<title>SINGAPORE: India tenders to sell end Mar naphtha from Madras.</title>
<headline>India tenders to sell end Mar naphtha from Madras.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) is offering by tender 27,000 tonnes of high aromatic naphtha (HAN) lifting March 27-29 from Madras on the east coast, industry sources said on Monday.</p>
<p>The tender closes March 20 and is valid for a day.</p>
<p>IOC's last HAN cargo from Madras which lifted January 5-7 was awarded at a $16.65 per tonne discount to Japanese spot quotes, on a free-on-board basis.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-8703086)</p>
